1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,500
Good morning and welcome again to Your City Today.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:08,660
With me today is Graham Campbell, a councillor from the city council.

3
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:13,286
He will be telling us about the plan to improve the fast-growing suburb of

4
00:00:13,286 --> 00:00:14,050
Red Hill.

5
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:16,300
Good morning Graham and welcome to the show.

6
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:17,000
Good morning, Carol.

7
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,455
Now, Graham, I understand that there has been a lot of community consultation for

8
00:00:22,455 --> 00:00:23,300
the new plan?

9
00:00:23,300 --> 00:00:27,417
Yes, we've tried to address some of the concerns that local groups told us

10
00:00:27,417 --> 00:00:27,720
about.

11
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:31,498
People we've heard from are mainly worried about traffic in the area,

12
00:00:31,498 --> 00:00:36,100
and, in particular, the increasing speed of cars near schools.

13
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:39,484
They feel that it is only a matter of time before there is an

14
00:00:39,484 --> 00:00:41,680
accident as a lot of the children walk to the school.

15
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:44,817
So we're trying to do something about that.

16
00:00:44,817 --> 00:00:49,000
Another area of concern is the overhead power lines.

17
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,640
These are very old and a lot of people we spoke to asked if

18
00:00:52,640 --> 00:00:54,200
something could be done about them.

19
00:00:54,200 --> 00:00:59,654
Well, I'm happy to report that the power company have agreed to move the

20
00:00:59,654 --> 00:01:03,160
power lines underground at a cost of $800,000.

21
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:07,325
I think that will really improve the look of the area, as well as

22
00:01:07,325 --> 00:01:07,920
being safer.

23
00:01:07,920 --> 00:01:09,314
That's good to know,

24
00:01:09,314 --> 00:01:14,192
but will that mean an increase in rates for the local businesses in that

25
00:01:14,192 --> 00:01:14,540
area?

26
00:01:14,540 --> 00:01:18,793
Well, the power company have agreed to bear the cost of this themselves after

27
00:01:18,793 --> 00:01:20,920
a lot of discussion with the council.

28
00:01:20,920 --> 00:01:25,355
This is wonderful news as the council now has some extra funds for us

29
00:01:25,355 --> 00:01:28,840
to put into other things like tree planting and art work.

30
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:33,336
Now, we've also put together a map which we've sent out to all the

31
00:01:33,336 --> 00:01:34,620
residents in the area.

32
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:37,380
And on the map we've marked the proposed changes.

33
00:01:37,380 --> 00:01:42,427
Firstly, we'll plant mature pine trees to provide shelter and shade just to the

34
00:01:42,427 --> 00:01:44,950
right of the supermarket in Days Road.

35
00:01:44,950 --> 00:01:50,071
In order to address the traffic problems, the pavements on the corner of Carberry

36
00:01:50,071 --> 00:01:51,900
and Thomas Street be widened.

37
00:01:51,900 --> 00:01:56,360
This will help to reduce the speed of vehicles entering Thomas Street.

38
00:01:56,360 --> 00:02:01,260
We think it's very important to separate the local residential streets form the main

39
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:01,610
road.

40
00:02:01,610 --> 00:02:06,151
So the roadway at the entry of Thomas Street from Days Road will be

41
00:02:06,151 --> 00:02:06,800
painted red.

42
00:02:06,800 --> 00:02:10,991
This should mark it more clearly and act as a signal for traffic to

43
00:02:10,991 --> 00:02:11,590
slow down.

44
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:16,828
One way of making sure that the pedestrians are safe is to increase signage

45
00:02:16,828 --> 00:02:17,950
at the intersections.

46
00:02:17,950 --> 00:02:22,240
A 'keep clear' sign will be erected at the junction of Evelyn Street

47
00:02:22,240 --> 00:02:25,870
and Hill Street, to enable traffic to exit at all times.

48
00:02:25,870 --> 00:02:30,145
Something we're planning to do to help control the flow of traffic in the

49
00:02:30,145 --> 00:02:34,419
area is to install traffic lights half way down Hill Street where it crosses

50
00:02:34,419 --> 00:02:35,030
Days Road.

51
00:02:35,030 --> 00:02:40,264
Now, we haven't only thought about the cars and traffic, of course, there's also

52
00:02:40,264 --> 00:02:41,760
something for the children.

53
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:45,862
We're going to get school children in the area to research a local story,

54
00:02:45,862 --> 00:02:50,256
the life of a local sports hero perhaps,and an artist will incorporate that story

55
00:02:50,256 --> 00:02:54,358
into paintings on the wall of a building on the other side of Hill

56
00:02:54,358 --> 00:02:55,530
Street from the supermarket.

57
00:02:55,530 --> 00:03:00,456
And finally, we've agreed to build a new children's playground which will be at

58
00:03:00,456 --> 00:03:05,030
the other end of Hill Street close to the intersection with Carberry Street.

59
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:09,400
Wonderful, now, what's the next stage?

60
00:03:09,400 --> 00:03:11,640
Well, the final plan...
